BT /F2 20 Tf 54 760 Td (Leakage and Modeling Plan) Tj ET
0.15 w 54 739 m 558 739 l S
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 715 Td (Leakage Considerations) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 697 Td (Several strong-looking fields may be downstream of the thing we eventually want to predict. For) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 682 Td (example, credit balance, subscription type, total credits, or feature gating fields should not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 667 Td (be used to predict monetization if they are only known after monetization happens.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 641 Td (Recommended Prediction Setup) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 68 623 Td (- Use a time-windowed setup: first 24 hours or first N events as features, then predict later) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 68 608 Td (  activation or engagement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 68 591 Td (- Define activation behaviorally, for example: a user creates or uses a canvas, interacts with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 68 576 Td (  AI, uses tools/blocks, uploads files, or returns across sessions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 68 559 Td (- Keep the model explainable. Logistic regression, random forest, or gradient boosting can) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 68 544 Td (  work, but feature importance and actionable interpretation matter more than raw score.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 68 527 Td (- Evaluate with ROC-AUC, precision/recall, F1, and confusion matrix, but connect the results) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 68 512 Td (  back to product decisions.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 485 Td (Next Analytical Step) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 467 Td (For each grouped-null family, check which event values populate the group. This will validate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 452 Td (whether the inferred groups map to pageview events, AI events, credit events, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 437 Td (subscription/feature events. That validation directly supports the rubric categories for data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 422 Td (understanding, funnel design, transition logic, and leakage handling.) Tj ET
endstream
